    [Misc][Main2Main] Upgrade release to v0.31.0 with verified main compatibility (#18229)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Upgrade the release dependency from vLLM v0.30.0 to
    [v0.31.0](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/db9527a46873454610df6dbedf79a36d6bf1a7f6)
    while keeping the independently supported verified-main target at
    [c4df37d](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/c4df37dfcc7f72ca41cd43801a468526ecf99a2b).
    Rebase on latest Ascend main `c2382c6`, preserving the CPP profiling
    changes from #18622. The file mapping below describes the diff for
    `23c8b15` against `c2382c6`.
    
    The two targets have different APIs despite both being supported: retain
    version-dependent forwarding for profiling randomization, PP batch
    lengths, Mamba allocation, EPLB setup and encoder-only prefill
    admission. Remove obsolete 0.30 branches only where both targets now
    share the contract.
    
    | Contract | Verified main `c4df37d` | Release v0.31.0 `db9527a` |
    | --- | --- | --- |
    | Profiling | Parent calls omit `randomize_inputs` | Forward the flag
    through V1/V2/310P and MC2 |
    | PP batch state | No `max_seq_len_np` | Preserve the field in
    `AscendInputBatch` |
    | Mamba allocation | Parent has no `prefill_end` | Forward checkpoint
    boundary |
    | EPLB setup | Update existing state/communicator | Construct state from
    model and mapping |
    | Non-chunked prefill | Keep encoder-only budget exception | Keep
    release budget rejection |
    
    #### Changes organized by downstream file
    
    Upstream links identify the reason or contract being adapted. For
    existing main behavior that becomes common to both targets, the change
    is removal of the old release branch, not a new port of the complete
    upstream implementation. File links are pinned to this PR head; [the
    complete fixed
    diff](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/compare/c2382c67aa6be12f1c822733cd47d021f61b0b23...23c8b15c2709978463490b0e8531bf5f9f27b9c1)
    shows the exact edits.
    
