    BalanceScheduler scope: this PR folds the old queue branches and adapts
    encoder-only admission. Its baseline DP balancing, running-only
    snapshot/accounting and connector-snapshot cleanup remain; complete
    scheduler-body synchronization and a strict AST equivalence requirement
    are deferred. The baseline drift guard may skip and does not prove
    complete upstream equivalence.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    The default release dependency becomes vLLM v0.31.0; the verified-main
    pin remains unchanged. Fixed-token prompt scoring handles
    broadcast/strided IDs correctly and reports an explicit error when used
    with unsupported lmhead TP. Resumable Dyntra continuations retain
    upstream stop/queue behavior, and PD prompt-tail graph/Mamba metadata
    follow the supported upstream contracts.
    
